Apple is sending a large portion of its <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> engineers to a multi-week bootcamp to learn to code using AI, reports <em><a href="https://www.theinformation.com/articles/apple-sends-siri-staffers-coding-bootcamp-latest-shakeup-organization">The Information</a></em>. Apple's decision to teach its programmers to better use AI for coding comes just two months before Apple is expected to unveil a smarter, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/wwdc/">more capable version of Siri at WWDC</a>.<br/>
